id:                     E6404
trigger_tool:           Meson|Conan|C/C++ compiler|dependency metadata
phase:                  configure|compile|dependency-closure
error_signature:        dependency found but public header missing because package exports nested include layout
severity:               2
category:               build,conan,meson,headers,dependency,evidence
match_keywords:         SDL_net.h, __has_include, include/SDL2, dependency found, header layout, pkg-config Cflags
title:                  Header-layout fallback must preserve upstream include contracts

root_cause:             A dependency can be resolved by pkg-config and expose a valid library while installing a public header below a vendor or API-family subdirectory. If several consumer headers include the historical basename and the generated Cflags expose only the package include root, compilation fails at whichever translation unit is compiled first even though dependency().found() is true. Changing the dependency version or disabling the feature hides the mismatch rather than repairing the public contract.
affected_scope:        Cross-platform C/C++ consumers whose dependencies have published packages with nested include layouts that differ from upstream source conventions.
verification_cmd:      Bind the dependency package revision and generated include roots; verify the header at each candidate path; compile every production include site with the same ordered __has_include fallback; require the library and feature dependency to remain enabled.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           ordered-header-layout-fallback
rec_description:        Retain the canonical basename include first at every production boundary, then accept only the known API-family subdirectory path. Emit a hard compile error when neither path exists, so a missing dependency cannot silently become a disabled feature.
rec_command:            inspect generated Cflags and compile the original production include site against the published package
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               narrow source patch at the public include boundary

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      dependency-metadata-repair
fallback_description:   Repair generated pkg-config includedir only when the package metadata is demonstrably wrong and the repair can be scoped to the task; do not rewrite a valid package or copy headers into the consumer tree.
fallback_command:       use a task-local metadata normalizer with exact package and header readback
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:           Conan generate() metadata guard

forbid_1_pattern:       treat dependency().found() as proof that every public header is reachable
forbid_1_reason:        Meson can find a library through pkg-config while the compiler include path still misses a nested header directory.
forbid_1_consequence:   The failure appears late in unrelated source compilation and may be misdiagnosed as a toolchain or SDL version defect.
forbid_2_pattern:       copy a missing header into the application source tree|disable the feature to bypass the include
forbid_2_reason:        Both approaches break package ownership or silently remove production functionality.
forbid_2_consequence:   The resulting binary is not linked and tested against the declared dependency closure.

principles:             P005,P010,P013
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E6401]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

